# =====================================================================
#  UserExpandsFolder.ab
# =====================================================================
#  sentence   User Expand Folder
#  v4         toggleFolder(id)  — IMPLEMENTED, half of it
#             leftpanel_v4.html line 511.
#  triggers   click a folder row (line 427-431: select + toggle)
#             press Enter on a selected folder (line 886-889)
#             the chevron
#
#  v4 DOES NOT SPLIT THIS.  there is one function and it flips a
#  flag: expanded.has(id) ? delete : add (line 512-513).  the panel
#  has no "Expand Folder" menu item either — only "Expand All"
#  (lines 769 and 846).  tasks 29 and 30 in leftpanel_tasks.md both
#  point at that one flip.
#
#  the SENTENCE still splits, and it splits for a reason that has
#  nothing to do with today's code: expand and collapse are
#  different intentions with different consequences once the panel
#  remembers things.  "collapse the folder you just closed" is a
#  plausible system act; "expand it" is not.  the day collapse
#  starts doing something extra, the program is already here.
#
#  no `failed` result: Expand declares `ok` only (alphabet.ab).
#  a folder that will not appear is render.failed, once.

program UserExpandsFolder

sentence  User Expand Folder
enter     folder.expand.requested

step system expand folder
  catch folder.expand.ok goto Redraw
